\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O Happy band of pilgrims,
\par If onward ye will tread,
\par With Jesus as your Fellow,
\par To Jesus as your Head!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. O happy if ye labour
\par As Jesus did for men:
\par O happy if ye hunger
\par As Jesus hungered then!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. The Cross that Jesus carried,
\par He carried as your due:
\par The crown that Jesus weareth,
\par He weareth it for you.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. The faith by which ye see Him,
\par The hope in which ye yearn,
\par The love that through all troubles
\par To Him alone will turn,
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. The trials that beset you,
\par The sorrows ye endure,
\par The manifold temptations
\par That death alone can cure:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. What are they but His jewels
\par Of right celestial worth?
\par What are they but the ladder
\par Set up to heaven on earth?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. O happy band of pilgrims,
\par Look upward to the skies,
\par Where such a light affliction
\par Shall win you such a prize.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

